WEBVTT

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:13.380
"Hanamaru Kindergarten"

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:33.850
Tsuchida-kun, good morning.

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:36.290
Good morning.

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:38.110
Looks like you made it on time today.

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.550
Even I wouldn't show up late every day.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:42.690
Yamamoto-sensei.

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:45.590
Tsuchida-sensei, good morning.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:47.450
Good morning.

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:49.390
It's another beautiful day.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:50.360
It certainly is.

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:56.710
I'll do my best today as well!

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.100
As will I.

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:02.020
You're so transparent, Tsuchida-kun.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:05.310
That's easier said than done...

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:08.450
"A Hanamaru Slide"

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.820
This class is more chaotic than I thought it would be.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:15.360
Hey, Tsuchi.

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:17.450
What is it, Anzu-chan?

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:19.840
What's your favorite food?

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:21.310
My favorite food?

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.230
I guess I like...

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:24.310
Tsuchida-sensei!

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.010
What's this?

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:28.300
They're crayons.

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:30.250
I can see that.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.140
Why were these in my locker?

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:33.780
We'll use them when it's time to draw...

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.730
...so leave them in your locker for now.

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:37.900
Okay!

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:41.510
What's your favorite food, Tsuchi?

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:43.410
I wouldn't call it my favorite...

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:44.900
...but I guess I eat a lot of salmon lunches.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:46.860
It's only a convenience store lunch, though.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.290
Salmon lunch? Convenience store lunch?

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:52.090
What's a convenience store lunch?

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:54.270
Tsuchida-sensei, Yuna-chan is crying.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.270
Is that like a lunch box?

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:55.180
Yes, it is.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.070
What's wrong, Yuna-chan? Does your tummy hurt?

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:01.680
If your tummy doesn't hurt, then what is it?

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:06.610
This morning, our doggie...

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:11.450
When I was leaving home, our doggie...

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:12.350
Excuse me, Tsuchida-sensei.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:14.670
Oh, Nishikaze-sensei.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.890
Our delivery just arrived.

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:18.810
Could you help bring it in?

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.400
Yes, I'll be there in a minute.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:22.080
Okay.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:22.770
Hey, Tsuchi.

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:24.530
What's a salmon lunch?

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:27.260
It's a lunch box with salmon in it.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:29.400
So, what happened to your doggie?

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:32.330
Our doggie wasn't feeling well...

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.700
I like fried eggs.

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:33.990
...so I asked daddy and he said...

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:33.990
I like sweet ones.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:36.310
Tsuchida-sensei, I need to go to the bathroom!

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:37.180
The bathroom?

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:40.240
Kenji-kun, could you wait a minute?

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:41.000
I help my mommy cook.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:43.000
But I need to pee now!

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.070
I can't cook anything yet, though.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:45.250
Then what happened?

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:50.300
And now our doggie has to go to the hospital.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:50.850
I need to go to the bathroom soon.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:51.410
Hey, Tsuchi...

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:52.800
...are you busy right now?

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:55.010
Yeah, I would say I'm pretty busy.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:58.100
Can I go explore the kindergarten?

00:03:58.290 --> 00:03:59.350
Yeah, sure.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:00.520
Okay!

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:03.350
Hey Koume-chan, Hii-chan.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:05.760
Let's go explore the kindergarten.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:06.820
Explore?

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:07.640
Can we do that?

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:09.920
Tsuchi said we could go.

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.690
There are classrooms on the second floor, too.

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:25.020
They look like the second years' classrooms.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:26.470
What is that?

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:29.330
I'm first!

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:30.160
Wait, Ken-chan!

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:41.240
I know, this must be a slide.

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:44.690
I'm going to try sliding!

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:46.320
Me too!

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:56.480
The ground is so far...

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:59.110
It's scary...

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:03.690
I think we're too young for this slide.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:07.370
If you say so, Anzu-chan.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:13.920
Look at all the teakettles!

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:18.930
Look at all the books!

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:23.510
What is this room?

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:30.210
Wow, looks like fun!

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.470
Let's go inside.

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:33.760
We might want to skip this one.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:37.140
It's okay. Tsuchi said we could.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:41.720
A festival decoration?

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:43.910
Let's get a closer look.

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:51.880
Anzu-chan, watch out.

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:53.220
You should come down.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:54.980
I'm fine.

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:06.140
Are you okay?

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:10.680
I'm fine.

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:15.530
We were lucky no one was injured...

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:19.610
...but as a rule, don't let the children out of your sight.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.260
I'm sorry.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:25.040
...so Karin-chan's parents will be picking her up early.

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:26.270
Got it.

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:36.200
I wonder what happened to Tsuchida-sensei.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.330
He must have made some kind of mistake.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:41.630
Things never go smoothly at first.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:43.540
I suppose you're right.

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:48.940
Listen up, everyone.

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:51.320
I have something to tell you before we eat lunch.

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:56.130
Make sure you tell a teacher before going anywhere other than the bathroom and the gym.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.190
Don't go running off without saying anything.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:02.670
Okay, I'll tell you when I go somewhere other than the gym!

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:07.560
But Anzu-chan's the one I'm most worried about...

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:13.810
Hey, why do you call Tsuchida-sensei "Tsuchi?"

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:16.640
You've been calling him that this whole time.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:17.520
Because...

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:18.460
Because what?

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:22.620
Because Tsuchi and I are lovers.

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:27.110
Lovers...

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:29.040
Wow.

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:32.520
That reminds me, there was talk of flirting at the entrance ceremony.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:36.840
Yup! It all started when Tsuchi hit on me.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:40.910
We have my parents' blessing, and we're dating with marriage in mind.

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:43.700
Her parents' blessing!

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:44.820
And they're going to get married.

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:47.350
No, no. None of that's true.

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:48.820
We're not getting married.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:50.400
We're not even dating.

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:54.080
Oh Tsuchi, you're so easily embarrassed.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:55.380
I'm not embarrassed.

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:57.430
He's turning red!

00:07:57.470 --> 00:07:58.600
No I'm not!

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:01.140
They're rather lively.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:05.220
That's what you call forbidden love.

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:06.570
Forbidden love?

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:07.790
That sounds cool!

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:10.020
It's not forbidden love.

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:10.740
He's panicking!

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.540
I have no intention of doing anything like that.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:11.960
He is!

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:17.630
Forbidden love! Forbidden love!

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:19.790
When are you getting married?

00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:22.780
F-forbidden love?

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:26.950
Strange rumors will make our families worry.

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:28.640
Please be careful.

00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:30.000
I'm sorry.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:34.360
And always remain calm when interacting with the children.

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:35.500
Yes.

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:38.650
Good grief.

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:40.060
Sorry, Tsuchi.

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:42.420
Oh, Anzu-chan.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:45.820
It's my fault the director got mad at you, right?

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:49.350
I guess it was too early to officially announce our relationship.

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:53.270
But I have no intention of dating you.

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:56.550
It's not your fault, Anzu-chan.

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:59.550
I just need to buckle down.

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:01.390
But...

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:02.640
What's wrong?

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:08.060
I thought I'd be a little better at this job.

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:09.960
It's odd.

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:11.710
It'll be okay.

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.500
If you try, you can do it.

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:17.890
After all, you're the man that will become my husband someday.

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:19.420
Th-thanks...

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:21.790
A kindergarten student cheered me up.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:25.180
Why am I telling my problems to a kindergarten student, anyway?

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:29.830
My mommy tells me I can do it if I try all the time.

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:31.370
Oh, really?

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:32.470
Tsuchida-kun!

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:40.010
Some of my students want to play ball with you.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:41.840
Do you think you could play with them for a bit?

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:43.530
Tsuchida-sensei!

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:45.000
Let's play!

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:49.130
Do you think Tsuchida-kun is going to be alright?

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:51.980
I have high hopes for Tsuchida-kun.

00:09:52.350 --> 00:09:54.140
He may be unreliable now...

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:57.000
...but I'm looking forward to seeing what kind of class he'll make.

00:09:57.140 --> 00:09:58.470
What kind of class?

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:02.490
At our kindergarten, each class epitomizes its teacher's personality.

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:06.540
The athletic Kusano-sensei's students are all active.

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:08.480
Now that you mention it...

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:14.170
The laid back Nishikaze-sensei's students are all laid back.

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:19.610
Kakogawa-sensei's students are all mature.

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:24.130
Yamamoto-sensei's students have a warm feeling.

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:28.620
I wonder how Tsuchida-kun's class will resemble him.

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:33.280
Director, you didn't mention my class just now.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:37.920
I suppose your class lacks composure.

00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:39.920
What? How can you say that?

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:42.940
You're amazing, Tsuchi!

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:44.400
You're not too bad at this.

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:45.260
Is that so?

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:48.250
Okay, now throw it as hard as you can.

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:49.600
Okay.

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:53.100
Easy.

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:56.510
There's Tsuchida-sensei!

00:10:56.960 --> 00:11:00.730
That's not fair! You can't just play with another class!

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:02.320
Play with us, too!

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:05.790
He's right.

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:08.910
Hey Tsuchi, play with us too!

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:10.990
Oh, right.

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:13.630
I guess we haven't played together yet.

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:16.710
Alright, let's play!

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:21.490
The Sakura Class hasn't been on the slide yet, has it?

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:24.260
Hanamaru Kindergarten is famous for it.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:25.950
The slide?

00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:31.940
Tsuchi...

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:34.890
Don't worry. I'll slide with you.

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:37.470
Really? Then I'm first!

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:44.830
Ready? Let's go.

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:45.740
Okay.

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:56.330
Anzu!

00:11:57.130 --> 00:11:58.220
Are you having fun?

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:00.630
Yes!

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:09.930
That looks fun.

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:11.730
Wait here, Anzu.

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:12.930
Okay.

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:21.000
Sensei, can we slide by ourselves if we want?

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:21.940
Yeah, sure.

00:12:29.550 --> 00:12:30.430
Tsuchida-kun...

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:32.930
...looks like you've finally gotten the hang of it.

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:38.300
Mommy!

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.810
Someone's in a good mood today.

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:42.920
Did something good happen?

00:12:43.230 --> 00:12:45.670
Yeah! Something wonderful happened!

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:49.330
Anzu must have really enjoyed that slide.

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:49.470
Today...

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:52.690
...Tsuchi addressed me without an honorific!

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:54.120
Is that what she's happy about?

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:03.210
...and I got a bunny as a birthday present.

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:04.990
Wow, lucky.

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:05.860
Is it cute?

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:08.790
It's cute and fluffy.

00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:11.550
Mr. Bunny is home alone today.

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:14.260
I want to go home and keep him company.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:16.010
Poor rabbit.

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:19.830
What do you mean?

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:22.520
Rabbits die if they're lonely.

00:13:22.850 --> 00:13:25.000
It might even be dead by the time you get home.

00:13:26.810 --> 00:13:30.260
Hey! Stop teasing Koume-chan with your nonsense!

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:33.200
I know who you are!

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:38.990
You're the second year from Sunflower Class that picks on everyone with big words, uh...

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:40.200
Kenji.

00:13:40.580 --> 00:13:41.860
And I'm not teasing anyone.

00:13:41.860 --> 00:13:43.760
I'm just stating the truth.

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:46.830
If anything, that girl is bullying her rabbit.

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:47.940
Bullying?

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:51.930
Yeah. Rabbits die from loneliness, and she left hers alone.

00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:56.000
If you keep talking, I'll hit you!

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:57.890
You shouldn't use violence.

00:13:58.010 --> 00:13:59.810
I'll tell on you.

00:13:59.910 --> 00:14:01.530
Ken-chan, you're so smart.

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:02.510
Wow!

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:04.420
Her rabbit won't die.

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:07.840
Hii-chan!

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:10.180
"A Hanamaru Genius"

00:14:10.590 --> 00:14:13.630
A lot of people say rabbits die from loneliness...

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:14.800
...but there's no evidence.

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:16.560
They can stay home alone.

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:20.120
With proper care, rabbits will live a long time.

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:23.290
So it's fine, okay?

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:25.060
R-really?

00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:27.370
Oh, good.

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:29.550
Really?

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:31.830
Cheeky first year.

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:33.180
Did you know?

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:37.160
If the roots of your nails aren't white, you're unhealthy.

00:14:37.450 --> 00:14:38.720
You might be sick.

00:14:39.010 --> 00:14:40.030
I don't have any...

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:42.700
I barely have any.

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:44.960
That's irrelevant to your health.

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:47.920
The white part is called your lunula...

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.660
...and it's freshly formed nail.

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:52.390
You cheeky first year.

00:14:52.770 --> 00:14:55.290
I used to be the most knowledgeable.

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:57.680
There's no way she's smarter than me.

00:14:58.350 --> 00:14:59.610
What are you guys doing?

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:03.580
That kid from the Sunflower Class is, um...

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:05.390
Hii-chan is amazing!

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:07.160
Oh, really?

00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:08.790
Have you heard of "gamer's brain?"

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:12.730
If you play too many games, you become stupid and short-tempered.

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:15.980
But I love games.

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:18.540
That hasn't been medically proven.

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:23.420
In fact, playing a little bit provides positive stimulation for the brain.

00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:25.530
Whew!

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:29.120
Of course, people who play ten hours a day would be out of the question.

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:33.280
I'll tell her something that will blow her socks off.

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:34.350
I know!

00:15:35.470 --> 00:15:39.300
That panda-cat you guys like so much doesn't actually exist!

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:41.480
I know.

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:43.560
Panda-cat is a cartoon.

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:47.400
It goes without saying imaginary characters do not actually exist.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:49.350
That's common knowledge.

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:50.110
Yeah.

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:53.900
Hiiragi, did you make some second year friends?

00:15:54.230 --> 00:15:55.190
Looks like it.

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:56.780
No you didn't!

00:15:56.940 --> 00:15:58.150
I'll make you regret this!

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:07.110
Damn it.

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:08.840
What does she think she is?

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:13.780
She's got to have some kind of weakness.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:16.550
I'll find that weak spot.

00:16:17.460 --> 00:16:19.690
Ken-chan, you're like a stalker.

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:22.280
Do you like that girl?

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:23.480
Shut up!

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:28.130
Have you heard the rumor about the forest near the west park?

00:16:28.310 --> 00:16:29.080
Yeah.

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:31.400
They say ghosts come out at night.

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:32.880
Ghosts?

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:33.900
Really?

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:37.280
It's true. My next door neighbor saw one.

00:16:37.290 --> 00:16:38.550
I'm scared.

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:39.260
Ghosts...

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:41.410
That could be interesting.

00:16:41.740 --> 00:16:43.850
Do ghosts really exist?

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:44.890
Well...

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:46.870
You're stupid!

00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:50.350
Ghosts are unscientific. There's no way they exist.

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:55.570
Ghosts have not been scientifically proven to exist...

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:57.520
...but it hasn't been disproven...

00:16:57.190 --> 00:16:57.930
Alright.

00:16:58.270 --> 00:16:59.950
We'll go to that forest tonight.

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:02.690
Whoever discovers the true identity of the ghost first wins.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:06.470
You shouldn't do that.

00:17:06.780 --> 00:17:08.670
Your parents would be worried.

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:10.170
You too, Hiiragi.

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:10.860
Okay.

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:12.310
I won't do it either.

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:13.400
Good, good.

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:16.190
"Faculty Office"

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:16.190
A walking encyclopedia?

00:17:16.670 --> 00:17:18.170
Isn't that a bit of an exaggeration?

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:21.200
Not at all. She really does know a lot.

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:25.110
Today, she was explaining that gamer's brain hasn't been medically proven...

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:27.680
Medically? Gamer's brain?

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:32.010
And she was telling us the white part of your nails is called the lunula.

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:34.410
Hiiragi-chan really is amazing.

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:36.960
She's always reading challenging books for adults.

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:38.510
Is that so?

00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:43.580
My class' Kenji-kun has been very interested in that Hiiragi-chan lately.

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:45.670
Oh, that boy?

00:17:46.150 --> 00:17:48.380
He was saying something to Hiiragi...

00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:51.940
Tsuchida-sensei, what is Hiiragi-chan's household like?

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:55.360
Her father is an astronomer.

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:59.470
I'm not sure if it's related, but she reads a lot.

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:01.840
She even reads her father's books.

00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:03.110
Really?

00:18:03.570 --> 00:18:07.040
Apparently, she frequently helps her father with his work.

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:09.090
Thanks for your help, Hii.

00:18:09.550 --> 00:18:12.120
I'm almost done with the orbital calculations.

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:13.720
That's...

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:15.310
How impressive.

00:18:15.770 --> 00:18:19.940
The other day, she corrected the kanji on my handout.

00:18:20.230 --> 00:18:22.510
Tsuchida-kun, are you okay?

00:18:27.110 --> 00:18:30.240
I'll expose the identity of the ghost first.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:33.650
That'll bring her down a notch.

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:37.800
Hello?

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:39.880
Good evening, Kusano-sensei.

00:18:41.630 --> 00:18:43.280
Kenji-kun is missing?

00:18:45.860 --> 00:18:48.240
Kusano-sensei, I think I know where he is.

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:49.690
I'll go look for him.

00:18:50.390 --> 00:18:52.080
I'll call you as soon as I find him.

00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:54.670
Hiiragi? She's here.

00:18:55.560 --> 00:18:57.080
She's reading. Why?

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:02.410
It's pretty dark inside this forest.

00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:09.310
What am I scared for?

00:19:09.860 --> 00:19:11.430
Ghosts don't exist.

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:17.000
There's no way something so unscientific could...

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:50.050
Found you.

00:19:52.130 --> 00:19:54.220
You? Why?

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:56.760
I heard you were missing from Tsuchida-sensei.

00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:58.960
I was worried, so I came too.

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:02.230
I heard screaming, so I thought you would be here.

00:20:03.270 --> 00:20:05.170
The ghost appeared!

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:06.180
Over there!

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:14.550
This is probably the true identity of the ghost you saw.

00:20:14.970 --> 00:20:16.800
You mistook it for a ghost in the dark.

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:19.030
I see...

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:24.870
Now that I'm calm, I can see it's just a bunch of garbage.

00:20:25.100 --> 00:20:27.430
This place is very important to me.

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:29.130
Important?

00:20:30.030 --> 00:20:33.100
I used to come here to look at stars with my father.

00:20:34.180 --> 00:20:36.680
It was our special place.

00:20:37.070 --> 00:20:38.800
I'm sad to see it in this state.

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:43.680
I'm supposed to meet Tsuchida-sensei in the park.

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:44.870
Let's go.

00:20:45.460 --> 00:20:48.060
S-sure, um...

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:50.110
Which way is the park?

00:20:50.800 --> 00:20:51.510
That way.

00:20:51.860 --> 00:20:53.110
How do you know?

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:55.730
The stars.

00:20:58.510 --> 00:21:04.000
People of the past used the stars to guide them.

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:05.830
Constellations, huh?

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:12.000
Hii!

00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:14.480
Hey!

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:16.370
Are you okay?

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:26.100
I admit defeat.

00:21:26.610 --> 00:21:28.100
Not only in knowledge.

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:31.270
You braved danger to save me.

00:21:31.590 --> 00:21:34.200
Not only that, but you use your knowledge for practical purposes.

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:36.250
I've got a long way to go.

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:39.470
Please take me on as a student, master!

00:21:39.800 --> 00:21:41.100
M-master?

00:21:41.520 --> 00:21:43.960
I'll work for you, master.

00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:46.630
I'll start by cleaning up the garbage in that forest.

00:21:47.730 --> 00:21:49.300
Hii-chan is a master?

00:21:49.430 --> 00:21:51.010
Wow!

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:53.200
What a peculiar situation.

00:21:53.490 --> 00:21:56.620
Master, that cat cosplay looks great.

00:23:30.900 --> 00:23:31.850
How are you?

00:23:31.850 --> 00:23:34.870
Somehow, I've become a master.

00:23:35.030 --> 00:23:37.010
You never know what will happen.

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:39.200
Go ahead, Tsuchida-sensei.

00:23:39.300 --> 00:23:40.200
Leave it to me.

00:23:40.270 --> 00:23:43.760
The next episode is about a love triangle and Yamamoto-sensei's day.

00:23:42.300 --> 00:23:43.530
"A Hanamaru Love Triangle"

00:23:43.530 --> 00:23:44.700
"A Hanamaru Day"

00:23:43.760 --> 00:23:44.700
See you then.

00:23:44.700 --> 00:23:49.490
"See you next time!"
